From 15de307f8d250499f4c4659cb51c8a33b0fd9580 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:52:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] privacy note: a log is kept on the system, filtered, unless
 its upload is chosen

The note of this build at the head of the privacy policy said that
"Submit Log" of LibreELEC's settings sends the log to the paste service
of LibreELEC. In this build those settings ask where the log goes, and
keep it on the system, after the filter of the diagnostics, unless the
upload is chosen (a patch of the settings add-on, in the LibreELEC
tree): the note says so, and that an upload goes as it is.
---
 privacy-policy.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/privacy-policy.txt b/privacy-policy.txt
index 1dce1ba..b46ba33 100644
--- a/privacy-policy.txt
+++ b/privacy-policy.txt
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ What it contacts when you use it:
 
     • If you make a library of films, series or music, the information providers that come with Kodi ask their services for what they show: The Movie Database, fanart.tv, TheAudioDB, MusicBrainz, AllMusic and others.
     • If you play an audio CD, Kodi asks gnudb.org for its titles. A setting in Settings, Player, Discs turns that off.
-    • If you tell the settings of LibreELEC to send a log (System, Submit Log), the log goes to the paste service of LibreELEC (paste.libreelec.tv) and is kept there under the address that you are shown. Nothing is sent before you choose that.
+    • If you tell the settings of LibreELEC to send a log (System, Submit Log), they ask where it goes. Kept on this system, which is what they offer first, it goes nowhere: it is written to the storage of the system (your drive; memory where the system keeps its storage there, as in live mode) after a filter that cuts addresses down to their server, takes out what it takes for a key or a password, and leaves out the lines that are too long for it. Uploaded, it goes as it is to the paste service of LibreELEC (paste.libreelec.tv) and is kept there under the address that you are shown. Nothing is sent before you choose that.
     • Whatever the add-ons that you install contact.
 
 Those servers see your network address and what the program that asks says of itself. The media centre says "Kodi" with its version and "LibreELEC" with its own: to them this build looks like Kodi on LibreELEC. Their own privacy policies apply to that.
